IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`
IMPORT `sfaa-div1-interpretation`
IMPORT `sfaa-div3-reit`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, Part 7 Division 3 (sections 137Y to 137ZC): the directors and chief executive officer of the responsible person for a real estate investment trust, the holders of
-- voting shares in the responsible person, and the responsible person's own disclosure. Several sections mirror Division 1 (sections 133, 134, 136 and 137G) and are generated
-- from Division 1's sources with the words changed and the text of THIS Division quoted. Business days are counted by sfa-periods.l4 (P8).

§ `s 137Y: duty of a director and chief executive officer of the responsible person to notify of interests`

-- src:30514 | 137Y.—(1) Every director and chief executive officer of the
-- src:30515 | responsible person for a real estate investment trust must give
-- src:30516 | written notice to the responsible person of particulars of —
-- src:30518 | (a) units in the trust, being units held by him or her, or in which
-- src:30519 | he or she has an interest and the nature and extent of that
-- src:30520 | interest;
-- src:30522 | (b) debentures or units of debentures of the trust which are
-- src:30523 | held by him or her, or in which he or she has an interest and
-- src:30524 | the nature and extent of that interest;
-- src:30526 | (c) such other securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:30527 | or units in a collective investment scheme as the Authority
-- src:30528 | may prescribe, which are held, whether directly or
-- src:30529 | indirectly, by him or her, or in which he or she has an
-- src:30530 | interest and the nature and extent of that interest; and
-- src:30532 | (d) any change in respect of the particulars of any matter
-- src:30533 | referred to in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c).
@ref s 137Y(1) (src:30514-30533)
GIVEN
    `the body is the responsible person for a real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the responsible person for a real estate investment trust within section 137S?
    `the person is a director of the responsible person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director of the responsible person (as section 2(1) defines "director")?
    `the person is a chief executive officer of the responsible person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the chief executive officer of the responsible person (as section 2(1) defines "chief executive officer")?
    `the person holds or has an interest in the matter, or the particulars of it have changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person hold, or have an interest in, the matter (or have the rights, options or contracts), or have the particulars of it changed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137Y(1) the director or chief executive officer must give the responsible person written notice of the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the body is the responsible person for a real estate investment trust`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the responsible person for a real estate investment trust"; the body is not one
        IF NOT (`the person is a director of the responsible person` OR `the person is a chief executive officer of the responsible person`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every director and chief executive officer of the responsible person"
        IF NOT `the person holds or has an interest in the matter, or the particulars of it have changed`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "units in the trust, being units held by him or her, or in which he or she has an interest"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Subsection (3)(a): the form and information are the Authority's to prescribe, so what they are is an input.
-- src:30539 | (a) must be in such form and must contain such information as
-- src:30540 | the Authority may prescribe; and
@ref s 137Y(2)(a) (src:30539-30540)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has prescribed the form and the information for the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed a form for the notice and the information it must contain?
    `the notice is in the form the Authority prescribes and contains the information it prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice in the form the Authority has prescribed, and does it contain the information the Authority has prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137Y(2)(a) the notice is in the form and contains the information the Authority prescribes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Authority has prescribed the form and the information for the notice`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "as the Authority may prescribe"
        IF `the notice is in the form the Authority prescribes and contains the information it prescribes`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be in such form and must contain such information as the Authority may prescribe"

-- Subsection (3)(b): the time. (i) a change: 2 business days after the person becomes aware (s 130(6) fixes when a person "becomes aware");
-- (ii) any other case: 2 business days after the LATER of (A) becoming director or chief executive officer and (B) becoming a holder of, or acquiring an interest in, the matter.
-- src:30542 | (b) must be given —
-- src:30544 | (i) in the case of a notice under subsection (1)(d), within
-- src:30545 | 2 business days after the director or chief executive
-- src:30546 | officer becomes aware of the change; or
@ref s 137Y(2)(b)(i) (src:30542-30546)
GIVEN
    `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person actually become aware of the fact or occurrence?
    `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of the fact or occurrence if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of their affairs?
    `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which dates in the period were there public holidays in Singapore? (Saturdays and Sundays are counted automatically.)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 137Y(2)(b)(i) the last day for the notice of a change` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a number of business days after` (`s 130(6) the day from which the person is taken to have been aware` `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence`) 2 `the public holidays`

-- src:30551 | (ii) in any other case, within 2 business days after —
-- src:30553 | (A) the date on which the director or chief
-- src:30554 | executive officer becomes such a director or
-- src:30555 | chief executive officer; or
-- src:30557 | (B) the date on which the director or chief
-- src:30558 | executive officer becomes a holder of, or
-- src:30559 | acquires an interest in, the units, debentures,
-- src:30560 | units of debentures, other securities,
-- src:30561 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or units
-- src:30562 | in a collective investment scheme referred to in
-- src:30563 | subsection (1),
-- src:30565 | (ii) whichever last occurs.
@ref s 137Y(2)(b)(ii) (src:30551-30565)
GIVEN
    `the day the person becomes director or chief executive officer` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person become a director or chief executive officer of the corporation?
    `the day the person becomes a holder of, or acquires an interest in, the matter` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person become a holder of, or acquire an interest in, the matter?
    `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which dates in the period were there public holidays in Singapore? (Saturdays and Sundays are counted automatically.)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 137Y(2)(b)(ii) the last day for any other notice` MEANS
    -- "whichever last occurs": the later of the two dates starts the 2 business days
    IF `the day the person becomes a holder of, or acquires an interest in, the matter` GREATER THAN `the day the person becomes director or chief executive officer`
    THEN `period: the last day of a number of business days after` `the day the person becomes a holder of, or acquires an interest in, the matter` 2 `the public holidays`
    ELSE `period: the last day of a number of business days after` `the day the person becomes director or chief executive officer` 2 `the public holidays`

-- src:30542 | (b) must be given —
-- src:30544 | (i) in the case of a notice under subsection (1)(d), within
-- src:30545 | 2 business days after the director or chief executive
-- src:30546 | officer becomes aware of the change; or
-- src:30551 | (ii) in any other case, within 2 business days after —
-- src:30553 | (A) the date on which the director or chief
-- src:30554 | executive officer becomes such a director or
-- src:30555 | chief executive officer; or
-- src:30557 | (B) the date on which the director or chief
-- src:30558 | executive officer becomes a holder of, or
-- src:30559 | acquires an interest in, the units, debentures,
-- src:30560 | units of debentures, other securities,
-- src:30561 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or units
-- src:30562 | in a collective investment scheme referred to in
-- src:30563 | subsection (1),
-- src:30565 | (ii) whichever last occurs.
@ref s 137Y(2)(b) (src:30542-30565)
GIVEN
    `the notice is of a change in the particulars of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice of a change in the particulars of that matter (paragraph (g))?
    `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person actually become aware of the fact or occurrence?
    `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of the fact or occurrence if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of their affairs?
    `the day the person becomes director or chief executive officer` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person become a director or chief executive officer of the corporation?
    `the day the person becomes a holder of, or acquires an interest in, the matter` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person become a holder of, or acquire an interest in, the matter?
    `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given?
    `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which dates in the period were there public holidays in Singapore? (Saturdays and Sundays are counted automatically.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137Y(2)(b) the notice is given in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice is given` AT MOST (IF `the notice is of a change in the particulars of the matter` THEN `s 137Y(2)(b)(i) the last day for the notice of a change` `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` `the public holidays` ELSE `s 137Y(2)(b)(ii) the last day for any other notice` `the day the person becomes director or chief executive officer` `the day the person becomes a holder of, or acquires an interest in, the matter` `the public holidays`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 2 business days after"; a period fixed in the text's own words (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a))


-- Subsection (6): "family member" means a spouse, or a son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter or stepdaughter below the age of 21 years.
-- Fork register A2: "below the age of 21 years" is read as limiting the children, not the spouse.
-- src:30581 | (4) In this section —
-- src:30583 | “family member” means a spouse, or a son, adopted son,
-- src:30584 | stepson, daughter, adopted daughter or stepdaughter below
-- src:30585 | the age of 21 years;
@ref s 137Y(4) (src:30581-30585)
GIVEN
    `the relation of the person to the director or chief executive officer` IS A `Family relation` @desc What is the person's relation to the director or chief executive officer?
    `the age of the relation in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is that relation, in years?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137Y(4) "family member" the person is a family member` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relation of the person to the director or chief executive officer`
    WHEN `a spouse` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a son` THEN `s 137Y(4) the child is below the age of 21 years` `the age of the relation in years`
    WHEN `an adopted son` THEN `s 137Y(4) the child is below the age of 21 years` `the age of the relation in years`
    WHEN `a stepson` THEN `s 137Y(4) the child is below the age of 21 years` `the age of the relation in years`
    WHEN `a daughter` THEN `s 137Y(4) the child is below the age of 21 years` `the age of the relation in years`
    WHEN `an adopted daughter` THEN `s 137Y(4) the child is below the age of 21 years` `the age of the relation in years`
    WHEN `a stepdaughter` THEN `s 137Y(4) the child is below the age of 21 years` `the age of the relation in years`
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a spouse, or a son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter or stepdaughter below the age of 21 years"

-- src:30581 | (4) In this section —
-- src:30583 | “family member” means a spouse, or a son, adopted son,
-- src:30584 | stepson, daughter, adopted daughter or stepdaughter below
-- src:30585 | the age of 21 years;
@ref 2 s 137Y(4) (the age limit on a child) (src:30581-30585)
GIVEN
    `the age of the relation in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is that relation, in years?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137Y(4) the child is below the age of 21 years` MEANS
    IF `the age of the relation in years` LESS THAN 21
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "below the age of 21 years"

-- Subsection (4)(a): a deemed interest. The text introduces it with "if", so a family member who holds nothing gives JUST FALSE (marginal reading (a), listed in NOTES.md);
-- the carve-out "(not being himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the responsible person)" and the defined term are limits in the text's own wording: NOTHING outside them.
-- src:30569 | (3) For the purposes of this section, a director or chief executive
-- src:30570 | officer of a responsible person is deemed to have an interest in
-- src:30571 | securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or units in a
-- src:30572 | collective investment scheme referred to in subsection (1) if a
-- src:30573 | family member of the director or chief executive officer (not being
-- src:30574 | himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the
-- src:30575 | responsible person) (as the case may be) has an interest in those
-- src:30576 | securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or units in a
-- src:30577 | collective investment scheme.
@ref s 137Y(3) (src:30569-30577)
GIVEN
    `the person is a family member of the director or chief executive officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 133(6) answer for the person (a spouse, or a child below 21)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the family member is himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the responsible person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the family member himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the responsible person?
    `the family member holds or has an interest in those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the family member hold, or have an interest in, those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137Y(3) the director or chief executive officer is deemed to have the family member's interest` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the person is a family member of the director or chief executive officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (NOT `the family member is himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the responsible person`) AND `the family member holds or has an interest in those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the person is a family member of the director or chief executive officer` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR `the family member is himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the responsible person`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a family member of the director or chief executive officer (not being himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the responsible person)"
        IF `the person is a family member of the director or chief executive officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to have an interest in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme referred to in subsection (1) if a family member"
        -- MARGINAL-READING (a): the deeming rule is introduced with "if"; a failed "if" is taken as the text's no. The other reading is NOTHING.
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer for "family member" was not given


-- Subsection (4), "unit" in relation to a debenture: "means" a right or interest in the debenture, "and includes" an option to acquire one. The definition is closed by "means",
-- so a thing that is neither is outside it.
-- src:30587 | “unit”, in relation to a debenture, means any right or interest,
-- src:30588 | whether legal or equitable, in the debenture, by whatever
-- src:30589 | name called, and includes any option to acquire any such
-- src:30590 | right or interest in the debenture.
@ref s 137Y(4) "unit" (src:30587-30590)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a right or interest, whether legal or equitable, in the debenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a right or interest, whether legal or equitable, in the debenture, by whatever name called?
    `the thing is an option to acquire a right or interest in the debenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an option to acquire any such right or interest in the debenture?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137Y(4) "unit" in relation to a debenture the thing is a unit` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a right or interest, whether legal or equitable, in the debenture` OR `the thing is an option to acquire a right or interest in the debenture`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any right or interest, whether legal or equitable, in the debenture, by whatever name called"

-- The regulative rule for the notice: the director or chief executive officer MUST give written notice within 2 business days (the clock of a trace counts business days
-- after the trigger; the dates are counted by the decision functions above). The party is an input so that one rule serves the director and the chief executive officer.
DECLARE `s 137Y action` IS ONE OF
    `s 137Y give the responsible person written notice`

-- src:30514 | 137Y.—(1) Every director and chief executive officer of the
-- src:30515 | responsible person for a real estate investment trust must give
-- src:30516 | written notice to the responsible person of particulars of —
-- src:30518 | (a) units in the trust, being units held by him or her, or in which
-- src:30519 | he or she has an interest and the nature and extent of that
-- src:30520 | interest;
-- src:30522 | (b) debentures or units of debentures of the trust which are
-- src:30523 | held by him or her, or in which he or she has an interest and
-- src:30524 | the nature and extent of that interest;
-- src:30526 | (c) such other securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:30527 | or units in a collective investment scheme as the Authority
-- src:30528 | may prescribe, which are held, whether directly or
-- src:30529 | indirectly, by him or her, or in which he or she has an
-- src:30530 | interest and the nature and extent of that interest; and
-- src:30532 | (d) any change in respect of the particulars of any matter
-- src:30533 | referred to in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c).
-- src:30537 | (2) A notice under subsection (1) —
-- src:30539 | (a) must be in such form and must contain such information as
-- src:30540 | the Authority may prescribe; and
-- src:30542 | (b) must be given —
-- src:30544 | (i) in the case of a notice under subsection (1)(d), within
-- src:30545 | 2 business days after the director or chief executive
-- src:30546 | officer becomes aware of the change; or
-- src:30551 | (ii) in any other case, within 2 business days after —
-- src:30553 | (A) the date on which the director or chief
-- src:30554 | executive officer becomes such a director or
-- src:30555 | chief executive officer; or
-- src:30557 | (B) the date on which the director or chief
-- src:30558 | executive officer becomes a holder of, or
-- src:30559 | acquires an interest in, the units, debentures,
-- src:30560 | units of debentures, other securities,
-- src:30561 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or units
-- src:30562 | in a collective investment scheme referred to in
-- src:30563 | subsection (1),
-- src:30565 | (ii) whichever last occurs.
@ref s 137Y(1) and (2) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:30514-30565)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137Y action`
`s 137Y(1) and (2) the director or chief executive officer must give written notice within 2 business days` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 137Y give the responsible person written notice`
    WITHIN 2
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "written notice was not given to the responsible person within 2 business days (section 137Y(2)(b))"


§ `s 137Z: penalties under Subdivision (2)`

-- The offences here are of "any director or chief executive officer of the responsible person"; only an individual is named, so one penalty serves.
-- src:30596 | 137Z.—(1) Any director or chief executive officer of the
-- src:30597 | responsible person for a real estate investment trust who —
-- src:30602 | (a) intentionally or recklessly contravenes section 137Y(1) or
-- src:30603 | (2); or
-- src:30605 | (b) in purported compliance with section 137Y, provides any
-- src:30606 | information which he or she knows is false or misleading
-- src:30607 | in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is,
-- src:30609 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:30610 | not exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:30611 | 2 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further
-- src:30612 | fine not exceeding $25,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:30613 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 137Z(1) (src:30596-30613)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 137Y(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 137Y(1) or (2)?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 137Y provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 137Y, did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137Z(1) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF ((`the person contravened section 137Y(1) or (2)` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 137Y provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("intentionally or recklessly contravenes section 137Y(1) or (2)" or "provides any information which he or she knows is false or misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is"), not that anyone else is innocent

@ref s 137Z(1) (the penalty) (src:30596-30613)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 137Z(1) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $250,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (24 months) or both; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
    Penalty OF 250000, 24, TRUE, 25000

-- src:30617 | (2) Any director or chief executive officer of the responsible person
-- src:30618 | for a real estate investment trust who —
-- src:30620 | (a) contravenes section 137Y(1) or (2); or
-- src:30622 | (b) in purported compliance with section 137Y, provides any
-- src:30623 | information which is false or misleading in a material
-- src:30624 | particular,
-- src:30626 | in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (1) shall be guilty
-- src:30627 | of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:30628 | $25,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:30629 | exceeding $2,500 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:30630 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 137Z(2) (src:30617-30630)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 137Y(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 137Y(1) or (2)?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 137Y provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 137Y, did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137Z(2) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person contravened section 137Y(1) or (2)` OR `the person in purported compliance with section 137Y provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("contravenes section 137Y(1) or (2)"), not that anyone else is innocent
        IF ((`the person contravened section 137Y(1) or (2)` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 137Y provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (i) "in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (1)": a case within subsection (1) is carved out of this one (a named complement)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 137Z(2) (the penalty) (src:30617-30630)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 137Z(2) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $25,000 and a further fine not exceeding $2,500 a day after conviction; no imprisonment is stated, so 0
    Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, 2500

-- src:30634 | (3) No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an
-- src:30635 | offence under this section after ––
-- src:30637 | (a) a court has made an order against the person for the
-- src:30638 | payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD in respect
-- src:30639 | of the same contravention; or
-- src:30641 | (b) the person has entered into an agreement with the
-- src:30642 | Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a
-- src:30643 | civil penalty under section 137ZD(4), in respect of the
-- src:30644 | same contravention.
@ref s 137Z(3) (src:30634-30644)
GIVEN
    `a court has made an order for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention?
    `the person has agreed with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137Z(3) no proceedings may be instituted for an offence under section 137Z` MEANS
    IF `a court has made an order for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention` OR `the person has agreed with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an offence under this section after"
    -- MARGINAL-READING (b): the bar is limited by its own wording ("after"); outside the limit the other reading is NOTHING.

§ `s 137ZA: duty of a holder of voting shares in the responsible person to notify the responsible person`

-- Subsection (3): the "percentage level": votes attached to the voting shares the person has an interest in, as a percentage of the votes attached to all the voting shares
-- (excluding treasury shares) in the responsible person or, where the share capital has 2 or more classes, in the class concerned, rounded DOWN to a whole number.
-- Fork register A4: the numerator is read as written ("all the voting shares in which the person has an interest"), whatever the class.
-- src:30670 | (3) In subsection (1), the percentage of interest of a person in the
-- src:30671 | voting shares in a responsible person for a real estate investment trust
-- src:30672 | is ascertained by expressing the total votes attached to all the voting
-- src:30673 | shares in which the person has an interest or interests immediately
-- src:30674 | before or (as the case may be) immediately after the relevant time, as
-- src:30675 | a percentage of the total votes attached to —
-- src:30677 | (a) all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the
-- src:30678 | responsible person; or
-- src:30680 | (b) where the share capital of the responsible person is divided
-- src:30681 | into 2 or more classes of shares, all the voting shares
-- src:30682 | (excluding treasury shares) in the class concerned,
-- src:30684 | and, if it is not a whole number, rounding that figure down to the next
-- src:30685 | whole number.
@ref s 137ZA(3) (src:30670-30685)
GIVEN
    `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in which the person has an interest or interests` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to all the voting shares in which the person has an interest or interests, immediately before or after the relevant time?
    `the share capital of the responsible person is divided into 2 or more classes of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the share capital of the responsible person divided into two or more classes of shares?
    `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the responsible person` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the responsible person?
    `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the class concerned` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the class concerned (leave 0 if the corporation has one class)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 137ZA(3) the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares` MEANS
    IF (IF `the share capital of the responsible person is divided into 2 or more classes of shares` THEN `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the class concerned` ELSE `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the responsible person`) AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE FLOOR ((`the total votes attached to all the voting shares in which the person has an interest or interests` TIMES 100) DIVIDED BY (IF `the share capital of the responsible person is divided into 2 or more classes of shares` THEN `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the class concerned` ELSE `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the responsible person`))


-- Subsection (1): "reaches, crosses or falls below 15%, 30%, 50% or 75%". The reading of the thresholds is that of section 137P(1) (fork register B11).
-- src:30657 | 137ZA.—(1) Where the percentage of interest of a person in the
-- src:30658 | voting shares in a responsible person for a real estate investment trust
-- src:30659 | reaches, crosses or falls below 15%, 30%, 50% or 75%, the person
-- src:30660 | must give written notice to the responsible person within 2 business
-- src:30661 | days after the person becomes aware of this.
@ref s 137ZA(1) (the thresholds) (src:30657-30661)
GIVEN
    `the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the percentage of interest (a whole number) of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person immediately before the relevant time?
    `the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the percentage of interest (a whole number) of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person immediately after the relevant time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 137ZA(1) the percentage of interest reaches, crosses or falls below 15%, 30%, 50% or 75%` MEANS
       ((`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time` LESS THAN 15) AND (`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time` AT LEAST 15))
    OR ((`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time` AT LEAST 15) AND (`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time` LESS THAN 15))
    OR ((`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time` LESS THAN 30) AND (`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time` AT LEAST 30))
    OR ((`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time` AT LEAST 30) AND (`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time` LESS THAN 30))
    OR ((`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time` LESS THAN 50) AND (`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time` AT LEAST 50))
    OR ((`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time` AT LEAST 50) AND (`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time` LESS THAN 50))
    OR ((`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time` LESS THAN 75) AND (`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time` AT LEAST 75))
    OR ((`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time` AT LEAST 75) AND (`the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time` LESS THAN 75))

-- src:30657 | 137ZA.—(1) Where the percentage of interest of a person in the
-- src:30658 | voting shares in a responsible person for a real estate investment trust
-- src:30659 | reaches, crosses or falls below 15%, 30%, 50% or 75%, the person
-- src:30660 | must give written notice to the responsible person within 2 business
-- src:30661 | days after the person becomes aware of this.
@ref s 137ZA(1) (src:30657-30661)
GIVEN
    `the body is the responsible person for a real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the responsible person for a real estate investment trust within section 137S?
    `the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the percentage of interest (a whole number) of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person immediately before the relevant time?
    `the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the percentage of interest (a whole number) of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person immediately after the relevant time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZA(1) the person must give the responsible person written notice of the change in the percentage of interest` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the body is the responsible person for a real estate investment trust`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a responsible person for a real estate investment trust"; the body is not one
        IF `s 137ZA(1) the percentage of interest reaches, crosses or falls below 15%, 30%, 50% or 75%` `the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time` `the percentage of interest of the person in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the percentage of interest of a person in the voting shares in a responsible person for a real estate investment trust reaches, crosses or falls below 15%, 30%, 50% or 75%"

-- src:30657 | 137ZA.—(1) Where the percentage of interest of a person in the
-- src:30658 | voting shares in a responsible person for a real estate investment trust
-- src:30659 | reaches, crosses or falls below 15%, 30%, 50% or 75%, the person
-- src:30660 | must give written notice to the responsible person within 2 business
-- src:30661 | days after the person becomes aware of this.
@ref s 137ZA(1) (src:30657-30661)
GIVEN
    `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person actually become aware of the fact or occurrence?
    `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of the fact or occurrence if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of their affairs?
    `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which dates in the period were there public holidays in Singapore? (Saturdays and Sundays are counted automatically.)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 137ZA(1) the last day for the notice` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a number of business days after` (`s 130(6) the day from which the person is taken to have been aware` `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence`) 2 `the public holidays`

@ref s 137ZA(1) (src:30657-30661)
GIVEN
    `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person actually become aware of the fact or occurrence?
    `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of the fact or occurrence if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of their affairs?
    `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given?
    `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which dates in the period were there public holidays in Singapore? (Saturdays and Sundays are counted automatically.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZA(1) the notice is given in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice is given` AT MOST `s 137ZA(1) the last day for the notice` `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` `the public holidays`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person must give written notice to the responsible person within 2 business days after the person becomes aware of this"; a period fixed in the text's own words (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a))

-- src:30665 | (2) A notice under subsection (1) must be in such form and must
-- src:30666 | contain such information as the Authority may prescribe.
@ref s 137ZA(2) (src:30665-30666)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has prescribed the form and the information for the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed a form for the notice and the information it must contain?
    `the notice is in the form the Authority prescribes and contains the information it prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice in the form the Authority has prescribed, and does it contain the information the Authority has prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZA(2) the notice is in the form and contains the information the Authority prescribes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Authority has prescribed the form and the information for the notice`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "as the Authority may prescribe"
        IF `the notice is in the form the Authority prescribes and contains the information it prescribes`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be in such form and must contain such information as the Authority may prescribe"

DECLARE `s 136 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 136 give the responsible person written notice of the change`


DECLARE `s 137ZA action` IS ONE OF
