-- src:30657 | 137ZA.—(1) Where the percentage of interest of a person in the
-- src:30658 | voting shares in a responsible person for a real estate investment trust
-- src:30659 | reaches, crosses or falls below 15%, 30%, 50% or 75%, the person
-- src:30660 | must give written notice to the responsible person within 2 business
-- src:30661 | days after the person becomes aware of this.
@ref s 137ZA(1) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:30657-30661)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137ZA action`
`s 137ZA(1) the person must give written notice within 2 business days` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 137ZA give the responsible person written notice`
    WITHIN 2
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "written notice was not given to the responsible person within 2 business days after the person became aware of the change (section 137ZA(1))"

§ `s 137ZB: penalties under Subdivision (3)`

-- src:30691 | 137ZB.—(1) Any person who —
-- src:30693 | (a) intentionally or recklessly contravenes section 137ZA(1)
-- src:30694 | or (2); or
-- src:30696 | (b) in purported compliance with section 137ZA, provides any
-- src:30697 | information which the person knows is false or misleading
-- src:30698 | in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is,
-- src:30703 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall —
-- src:30705 | (c) in the case of an individual, be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:30706 | not exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:30707 | exceeding 2 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:30708 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every
-- src:30709 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues
-- src:30710 | after conviction; or
-- src:30712 | (d) in the case of a corporation, be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:30713 | not exceeding $250,000 and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:30714 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every
-- src:30715 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues
-- src:30716 | after conviction.
@ref s 137ZB(1) (src:30691-30716)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 137ZA(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 137ZA(1) or (2)?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 137ZA provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 137ZA, did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZB(1) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF ((`the person contravened section 137ZA(1) or (2)` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 137ZA provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("intentionally or recklessly contravenes section 137ZA(1) or (2)" or "in purported compliance with section 137ZA, provides any information which the person knows is false or misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is"), not that anyone else is innocent

@ref s 137ZB(1) (the penalty) (src:30691-30716)
GIVEN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 137ZB(1) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an individual`
        THEN JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 24, TRUE, 25000)  -- a fine not exceeding $250,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (24 months) or both; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
        IF `the person is a corporation`
        THEN JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 0, FALSE, 25000)  -- a fine not exceeding $250,000, no imprisonment is stated, so 0; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an individual" and "in the case of a corporation" are the only cases the paragraphs name

-- src:30720 | (2) Any person who —
-- src:30722 | (a) contravenes section 137ZA(1) or (2); or
-- src:30724 | (b) in purported compliance with section 137ZA, provides any
-- src:30725 | information which is false or misleading in a material
-- src:30726 | particular,
-- src:30728 | in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (1) shall be guilty
-- src:30729 | of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:30730 | $25,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:30731 | exceeding $2,500 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:30732 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 137ZB(2) (src:30720-30732)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 137ZA(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 137ZA(1) or (2)?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 137ZA provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 137ZA, did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZB(2) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person contravened section 137ZA(1) or (2)` OR `the person in purported compliance with section 137ZA provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("contravenes section 137ZA(1) or (2)"), not that anyone else is innocent
        IF ((`the person contravened section 137ZA(1) or (2)` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 137ZA provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (i) "in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (1)": a case within subsection (1) is carved out of this one (a named complement)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 137ZB(2) (the penalty) (src:30720-30732)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 137ZB(2) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $25,000 and a further fine not exceeding $2,500 a day after conviction; no imprisonment is stated, so 0
    Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, 2500

-- src:30736 | (3) No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an
-- src:30737 | offence under this section after ––
