    `the day the responsible person became aware of the acquisition or disposal, or received the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the responsible person become aware of the acquisition or disposal, or receive the notice?
    `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which dates in the period were there public holidays in Singapore? (Saturdays and Sundays are counted automatically.)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 137ZC(1) the last day for the announcement` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a number of business days after` `the day the responsible person became aware of the acquisition or disposal, or received the notice` 1 `the public holidays`

@ref s 137ZC(1) (src:30786-30793)
GIVEN
    `the day the responsible person became aware of the acquisition or disposal, or received the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the responsible person become aware of the acquisition or disposal, or receive the notice?
    `the day the responsible person announced or disseminated the information` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the responsible person announce or disseminate the information to the organised market operated by the approved exchange?
    `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which dates in the period were there public holidays in Singapore? (Saturdays and Sundays are counted automatically.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZC(1) the announcement is made in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the responsible person announced or disseminated the information` AT MOST `s 137ZC(1) the last day for the announcement` `the day the responsible person became aware of the acquisition or disposal, or received the notice` `the public holidays`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no later than the end of the business day following the day on which the responsible person became aware of the acquisition or disposal, or received the notice"; a period fixed in the text's own words (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a))

DECLARE `s 137ZC action` IS ONE OF
    `s 137ZC announce or disseminate the particulars or the information stated in the notice`

-- src:30758 | 137ZC.—(1) Where the responsible person for a real estate
-- src:30759 | investment trust —
-- src:30761 | (a) acquires or disposes of interests in units in, or debentures
-- src:30762 | or units of debentures of, the real estate investment trust;
-- src:30764 | (aa) acquires or disposes of interests in such securities,
-- src:30765 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or units in a
-- src:30766 | collective investment scheme of the real estate
-- src:30767 | investment trust as may be prescribed by regulations
-- src:30768 | made under section 341; or
-- src:30770 | (b) has been notified in writing by —
-- src:30772 | (i) a substantial unitholder of the real estate investment
-- src:30773 | trust pursuant to a requirement imposed on the
-- src:30774 | substantial unitholder under section 135, 136 or 137
-- src:30775 | as applied by section 137U(1);
-- src:30777 | (ii) a director or chief executive officer of the
-- src:30778 | responsible person pursuant to a requirement
-- src:30779 | imposed on him or her under section 137Y; or
-- src:30781 | (iii) a person who holds an interest or interests in voting
-- src:30782 | shares in the responsible person pursuant to a
-- src:30783 | requirement imposed on the person under
-- src:30784 | section 137ZA,
-- src:30786 | the responsible person must announce or otherwise disseminate the
-- src:30787 | particulars of the acquisition or disposal, or the information stated in
-- src:30788 | the notice it received (as the case may be) to the organised market
-- src:30789 | operated by the approved exchange on whose official list any or all of
-- src:30790 | the units in the trust are listed, as soon as practicable and in any case
-- src:30791 | no later than the end of the business day following the day on which
-- src:30792 | the responsible person became aware of the acquisition or disposal, or
-- src:30793 | received the notice.
@ref s 137ZC(1) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:30758-30793)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137ZC action`
`s 137ZC(1) the responsible person must announce or disseminate the information by the end of the next business day` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 137ZC announce or disseminate the particulars or the information stated in the notice`
    WITHIN 1
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the particulars or the information were not announced or disseminated by the end of the business day following the day the responsible person became aware of the acquisition or disposal, or received the notice (section 137ZC(1))"

-- src:30800 | (2) The responsible person must announce or otherwise
-- src:30801 | disseminate the information in such form and manner as the
-- src:30802 | Authority may prescribe.
@ref s 137ZC(2) (src:30800-30802)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has prescribed the form and manner for announcing or disseminating the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed a form and manner for announcing or disseminating the information?
    `the responsible person has announced or disseminated the information in the form and manner the Authority prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the responsible person announced or disseminated the information in the form and manner the Authority prescribes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZC(2) the responsible person announces or disseminates the information in the form and manner the Authority prescribes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Authority has prescribed the form and manner for announcing or disseminating the information`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "in such form and manner as the Authority may prescribe"
        IF `the responsible person has announced or disseminated the information in the form and manner the Authority prescribes`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The responsible person must announce or otherwise disseminate the information in such form and manner as the Authority may prescribe"

-- src:30806 | (3) Any responsible person for a real estate investment trust that —
-- src:30808 | (a) intentionally or recklessly contravenes subsection (1) or
-- src:30809 | (2); or
-- src:30811 | (b) in purported compliance with this section, announces or
-- src:30812 | disseminates any information which the responsible person
-- src:30813 | knows is false or misleading in a material particular or is
-- src:30814 | reckless as to whether it is,
-- src:30816 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:30817 | not exceeding $250,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:30818 | further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every day or part of a day
-- src:30819 | during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 137ZC(3) (src:30806-30819)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 137ZC(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 137ZC(1) or (2)?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 137ZC announced or disseminated information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 137ZC, did the person announce or disseminate information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZC(3) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF ((`the person contravened section 137ZC(1) or (2)` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 137ZC announced or disseminated information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("intentionally or recklessly contravenes subsection (1) or (2)" or "in purported compliance with this section, announces or disseminates any information which the responsible person knows is false or misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is"), not that anyone else is innocent

@ref s 137ZC(3) (the penalty) (src:30806-30819)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 137ZC(3) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $250,000, no imprisonment is stated, so 0; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
    Penalty OF 250000, 0, FALSE, 25000

